<meta type=book>
<title | Config-driven contents — a book (#218)>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config toc=true toc-location=body />

<chapter | Counting Elephants>

For a book, the config-driven contents listing reflects the assembled whole-book
structure — chapters and their sections. Books are numbered by default, so the
listing shows each entry's number un-glued from its title ("1" then the title in
separate spans), not run together.

<sub-section | Aerial Transects>

A chapter section, listed beneath its chapter.

<sub-section | Ground Counts>

Another section.

<chapter | Browse Pressure>

A second chapter. (Book *navigation* — the chapter rail, prev/next, cover — is a
separate, deferred concern; `<config toc>` produces the contents listing, not that
reading-interface chrome.)
